# Post-synthesis formal equivalence: conv5x5_pe RTL vs its generic netlist.
#
# Every other check in this repo is RTL simulation: it compares the RTL against
# the Python golden model. None of them look at what synthesis produced. This
# proves, by SAT rather than by stimulus, that the netlist Yosys emits computes
# the same function as the RTL it was elaborated from -- for all inputs and all
# reachable states, not just the vectors a testbench happens to drive.
#
# "gold" is the RTL after elaboration only. "gate" is the same source through
# the full synth/yosys.ys flow. equiv_make pairs their signals, equiv_simple
# discharges the combinational points by SAT, equiv_induct proves the sequential
# ones by induction, and equiv_status -assert exits non-zero if a single point
# is left unproven -- that assert is what makes this a check rather than a report.
#
# Two things this flow needs that are easy to miss:
#   * async2sync, on BOTH sides. conv5x5_pe resets on rst_ni asynchronously, and
#     equiv_simple has no SAT model for an async FF -- without it the run dies
#     with "No SAT model available for async FF cell", not with a wrong answer.
#   * equiv_simple -short before the full equiv_simple. The short pass stops its
#     input cones at shared nodes and discharges most points cheaply, leaving far
#     fewer for the expensive full pass: 196s here versus minutes without it.

read_verilog -sv rtl/conv5x5_row_mac.sv
read_verilog -sv rtl/requantize.sv
read_verilog -sv rtl/conv5x5_pe.sv
hierarchy -check -top conv5x5_pe
proc
flatten
async2sync
opt_clean
design -stash gold

read_verilog -sv rtl/conv5x5_row_mac.sv
read_verilog -sv rtl/requantize.sv
read_verilog -sv rtl/conv5x5_pe.sv
hierarchy -check -top conv5x5_pe
proc
opt
fsm
opt
memory
opt
techmap
opt
flatten
async2sync
opt_clean
design -stash gate

design -copy-from gold -as gold conv5x5_pe
design -copy-from gate -as gate conv5x5_pe
equiv_make gold gate equiv
hierarchy -top equiv
equiv_simple -short
equiv_simple
equiv_induct
equiv_status -assert
